      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS present this fine three-bedroom terraced home to the Ballyfermot market. Located on the mature and highly popular Clifden Road, this property is in need of renovation throughout and offers a complete blank canvas with a great opportunity to make it your own and create the ultimate family home.\nThe location is second to none, with a wealth of local amenities on your doorstep including schools, shops, and sports clubs. Ballyfermot Village is just a short stroll away, offering excellent public transport links with frequent bus routes into Dublin City Centre. The M50 motorway, Naas Road, and Liffey Valley Shopping Centre are also easily accessible by car.\nInternal living accommodation of c. 70 sqm is laid out over two floors and packed with potential. On the ground floor, you are welcomed by an entrance hallway that leads into a spacious living room. To the rear is a kitchen space alongside the main family bathroom. This ground-floor layout offers massive scope to open up or extend the space to create a modern, open-plan kitchen and dining area. Upstairs, the property features three generous double bedrooms, providing excellent family living space. To the front is a well-maintained garden, while the rear boasts a standout feature: a large, sunny south-facing garden that acts as a complete sun trap, fully completed by three substantial block storage sheds.\nEarly viewing is highly advised. Call RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS today!\n\nAdditional Features;\n• c. 70 sqm\n• 3 bed / 1 bath\n• BER C\n• In of complete TLC\n• Blank canvas opportunity to modernise to your own taste\n• Large sunny south-facing rear garden\n• Three substantial block storage sheds to the rear\n• Well-maintained front garden\n• Living room, kitchen, and bathroom all on ground floor\n• Three generous double bedrooms upstairs\n• Highly sought-after, mature residential road\n• Ballyfermot Village within walking distance\n\nDirections\nFrom Ballyfermot Road, turn onto Kylemore Road heading toward the Naas Road. Take the right turn onto Landen Road, then turn left onto Clifden Road. Proceed straight down the road and No. 30 will be located on your right hand side."
      },
